ground_truth:
To link a voice agent to a section in your webpage using the `@humeai/voice-react` package, you need to follow these steps:

1. Install the package:

`npm install @humeai/voice-react`

2. Set up the VoiceProvider wrapper:

First, wrap your application (or the section where you want to use the voice agent) with the `VoiceProvider` component (1):

```import { VoiceProvider } from '@humeai/voice-react';

function App() {
  return (
    <VoiceProvider>
      {/* Your webpage content including the section with voice agent */}
      <YourPageContent />
    </VoiceProvider>
  );
}```

3. Create a voice-enabled component:

In the specific section where you want the voice agent, create a component that uses the `useVoice` hook (1):

```'use client';
import { useVoice } from '@humeai/voice-react';

export function VoiceSection({ accessToken }: { accessToken: string }) {
  const { connect, disconnect, status } = useVoice();

  return (
    <div className="voice-agent-section">
      <h2>Voice Agent</h2>
      <button
        onClick={() => {
          if (status.value === 'connected') {
            disconnect();
          } else {
            void connect({
              auth: { type: 'accessToken', value: accessToken },
              configId: '<YOUR_CONFIG_ID>',
              // other configuration props go here
            });
          }
        }}
      >
        {status.value === 'connected' ? 'End Call' : 'Start Voice Agent'}
      </button>
      {/* Add other voice-related UI elements here */}
    </div>
  );
}```

Important notes:
- The `connect()` function must be called from a user interaction (like a button click) due to browser audio policies (1)
- You'll need to provide your own `accessToken` and `configId` from your EVI configuration (1)
- The voice agent will only work in components that are children of the `VoiceProvider` (1)

This setup allows you to integrate the voice agent into any specific section of your webpage while maintaining proper state management through the React context system.
